588767" :question/math-academy-id "q-96628" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+x?$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,-1),(-2,-2),$ and $(1,1).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-1)}=(-2)^{2}+(-2)=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,-2)}=(-2)^{2}+(-2)=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,1)}=(1)^{2}+(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/21e88a2ac9e3c4e94e72f49e2c7635bf326b7a5ff2d8697c776e0d5eefc52b2a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5177f277-29a6-5df6-96c5-6bf53ffd9c51" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Possible Slope Field Based on the Type of Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f327c3cb-d503-545a-9532-5c130de0636b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/a69e37e076aded0627990fcb2d6a3c5e1bc2935ffc6337fee0cc7443c3fd17c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305945} {:answer/id #uuid "c38e1fcc-4972-50aa-8be5-8452e5d7c7a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040080/assets/6359148d1177fb4b583bd077b4b1df6153331b754f9ea8d092e4549d9d027e15.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305946} {:answer/id #uuid "a581a91b-9fbb-5887-a652-b9ed463d40e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :